  {"type": "split", "photo": "in", "reverse": True, "h2": "HVAC services in Woodbridge that keep a big house even, top to bottom",
   "html": "<p>Keeping a 3,000 or 4,000 square foot house comfortable isn't only about a bigger furnace. Size alone often makes it worse. A huge single-stage unit heats the rooms near the furnace room quickly, shuts off, and leaves the far bedrooms behind.</p>"
           "<p>What works is matching capacity to the house and controlling how it's delivered. We start with a Manual J load calculation, then check the duct system: the length of the runs, the size of the trunk and the number of returns on each floor. From there we choose between one variable-speed system with zoning, two systems split by floor, or a main system plus a ductless head for a room the ducts can't reach.</p>"
           "<p>Noise matters too in a busy house. Variable-speed blowers and inverter-driven heat pumps spend most of their time at low speed, so you hear far less from the vents and the outdoor unit.</p>"
           "<ul class=\"checklist\"><li>Midea MGH96 furnaces from 60,000 to 120,000 BTU, two-stage and variable-speed</li><li>Lennox ML296V and EL297V furnaces at 96% to 97% AFUE</li><li>Zoning with separate thermostats for floors or a suite</li><li>Cold-climate heat pumps from 2 to 5 tons</li></ul>"},
  {"type": "steps", "h2": "How our Woodbridge HVAC technicians plan a large system",
   "lead": "Bigger homes get more measuring up front. It saves money later.",
   "items": [
    {"title": "Hear from everyone who lives there", "text": "We ask who sleeps where, who runs warm or cold, and when the house is busiest. That tells us where zones make sense."},
    {"title": "Measure the house and the ducts", "text": "Room-by-room load calculation, airflow at the far registers, static pressure and panel capacity."},
    {"title": "Price one or two clear options", "text": "A guaranteed written quote with model numbers, the zone layout, a rebate estimate and financing choices."},
    {"title": "Install, balance each zone and hand over", "text": "We commission every zone, confirm airflow in the far rooms, program the thermostats and register the warranty."}]},
  {"type": "quote_split", "photo": "sys", "h2": "Furnace installation in Woodbridge sized for the whole family",
   "form_h3": "Tell us about your Woodbridge home",
   "html": "<p>Tell us how many floors the house has, how many people live there and which rooms cause the arguments. We'll come back with a guaranteed price on a system that fits the house, not simply the biggest unit available.</p>"
           "<p>Many families here pair the new furnace with a cold-climate heat pump. The heat pump handles cooling and most of the heating, and the gas furnace covers the coldest nights. Gas-heated homes may qualify for a heat pump rebate, commonly up to $2,000, with pre-approval before installation.</p>"
           "<ul class=\"checklist\"><li>Two-stage, variable-speed furnaces for quiet, even heat</li><li>Zoning for suites and separate floors</li><li>Rinnai tankless for busy mornings</li><li>0% financing for 3, 6 or 9 months, OAC</li></ul>"},
